  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Selected paths at 1 and 8 tokens",
      "items": [
        "T is batch times query length. T=1 selects Tiny; T=8 selects Tiny2. Both select @moe_helper0 with NW=8, WS=1 and WGS=0.",
        "The helper is physical warp 0 through the TIDX remap. The other eight physical warps compute. This is 288 threads, compared with 576 in B4/MAIN."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "A real barrier remains in the loop",
      "items": [
        "The selected WSB loop writes FP32 partials, executes fence.proxy.async.shared and bar.sync over 256 compute threads. Logical compute thread 0 then refills the released weight slot.",
        "The helper issues the initial remaining slots and consumes ordinary epilogues. It is not the sole steady-state weight producer. Activations stay in registers, so the WGS activation-ring drawing does not apply."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Tiny versus Tiny2",
      "items": [
        "Both have three weight slots, four partial buffers, FAST1=2 and final-item prefetch. Tiny handles up to four tokens; Tiny2 handles five through eight.",
        "The final two B units stay with compute warps in Tiny; one stays in Tiny2. Tiny disables L2 cache hints; Tiny2 keeps the default hints. These are source-selected policies, not new speed measurements."
      ]
    }
  ]
